<title>USA: Ingersoll-Rand in venture with India's Wadco.</title>
<headline>Ingersoll-Rand in venture with India's Wadco.</headline>
<dateline>WOODCLIFF, N.J. 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ingersoll-Rand Co said it formed a joint venture with India's Wadco Tools Ltd by buying a majority stake in Wadco for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Wadco makes pneumatic power tools and accessories for automotives, motorcycles and electrical appliances. It employs about 200 people, Ingersoll-Rand said.</p>
<p>The joint venture is part of Ingersoll-Rand's Production Equipment Group, the company added.</p>
